    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "I’ve always had a strong connection with mathematics, especially since I studied it in high school and continued through my bachelor’s. It’s not just a subject for me—it’s a language I use to understand patterns in nature, like in chemistry or even in how plants grow in my garden. I find it logical, beautiful, and deeply satisfying when I solve problems.",
    "Do you ever get anxious when thinking about mathematics?": "Occasionally, yes—especially when the problems get complex or time is limited. I’m not naturally anxious about math, but when I feel overwhelmed, like during exams or when I’m trying to grasp something new, my mind starts to race. That’s where I remind myself to breathe and break the problem into smaller parts, which helps me regain focus.",
    "Did you ever use AI to support your math learning in the last year? If yes, how was your experience?": "Yes, I used an AI tutor app last year to review calculus concepts. It explained step-by-step how to integrate functions and gave me practice problems with instant feedback. It was helpful, especially for visualizing graphs. However, I still needed to verify answers with my professor to ensure accuracy. It’s a useful tool, but not a replacement for human guidance.",
