    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can offer personalized tutoring, explain concepts in different ways, and generate practice problems tailored to a student’s level. They can also help students explore real-world applications of math, like in gardening or chemistry. However, they should complement—not replace—teachers. With proper guidance, they can make learning more accessible and less intimidating for students like me who are still building confidence."
